      "card_ids": ["C13"],
      "claim": "A 13C-lycopene study reported 23.2% bioavailability for all-trans lycopene, an above-threshold estimate, but this is an outlier relative to most lycopene systemic-availability measurements.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "The query is a large, highly lipophilic ubiquinone-like polyisoprenyl quinone. The closest structural analog, tocotrienol, has poor oral bioavailability, and lycopene data also support low systemic availability for this lipophilic isoprenoid class. High-bioavailability examples such as phytoene are less transferable because they lack the polar quinone head. Therefore F is more likely below 20%.",
